"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[3326],{93326:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"schemaVersion":1,"locale":"en","slug":"gajd-1-30-dnej","title":"Guide 1. A 30-day plan: 10 steps to mark off","sourceFingerprint":"43e8d98887675320b408a707db6afc086f383736fde2be8b6bead08a69bbd940","blocks":[{"id":"b001","markdown":"## A 30-day plan"},{"id":"b002","markdown":"10 steps to mark off"},{"id":"b003","markdown":"The whole module becomes 10 practical steps over roughly a month. You need not do everything in a day. Mark a step when complete. If it does not apply, for example you have no debt, mark it and continue. Each step cites the lesson with detail."},{"id":"b004","markdown":"### Step 1: Day 1. Calculate your hourly price"},{"id":"b005","markdown":"Divide take-home pay by working hours in the month, around 168 on average. Save the result in phone notes for judging a purchase’s real cost. Lesson 1."},{"id":"b006","markdown":"### Step 2: Day 2. Export 3 months of spending"},{"id":"b007","markdown":"Open every bank app where you have cards and export the last 3 months of transactions or use spending analytics. Add marketplace orders, cash and App Store or Google Play subscriptions. Combine in one table. Important: transfers between your accounts are not spending. Lesson 2."},{"id":"b008","markdown":"### Step 3: Day 3. Sort spending into 3 baskets"},{"id":"b009","markdown":"Mandatory, lifestyle and leaks. Calculate each basket’s average monthly amount and lesson 1’s runway: accessible savings divided by monthly expenses. The crucial figure is average monthly leaks. Lessons 1 and 2."},{"id":"b010","markdown":"### Step 4: Day 4. Close the leaks"},{"id":"b011","markdown":"Cancel subscriptions unused during the last month. Disable paid bank notifications and unnecessary services. Remove saved cards from apps where impulse buying happens most. Lesson 2."},{"id":"b012","markdown":"### Step 5: Day 5. Check credit history and set restrictions"},{"id":"b013","markdown":"Request credit history through Gosuslugi, free 2 times yearly per bureau, and confirm no unexplained debts exist. Restrict new borrowing, at least online and MFO lending. If no borrowing is planned soon, full restriction is better.\\nAlso restrict SIM contracts without personal attendance and check devices accessing Gosuslugi. Help parents arrange a trusted-person banking confirmation if unprotected against fraud. Important: an unknown loan requires immediate contact with the issuing bank and police. Lessons 4, 5 and 7."},{"id":"b014","markdown":"### Step 6: Day 6. Put all debts in one table"},{"id":"b015","markdown":"Skip if debt-free. Record lender, balance, full cost or rate, monthly payment and end date for each loan. Divide all payments by monthly income to calculate debt burden. Mark debts above 30% annually for first repayment. Lesson 5."},{"id":"b016","markdown":"### Step 7: Day 7. Open savings and automate transfers"},{"id":"b017","markdown":"Choose daily-balance savings, preferably outside your salary bank. The saving share is step 3’s leaks divided by income. With few leaks, begin at 3–5%. Automate the share on payday, or both dates if paid twice. Important: confirm deposit-insurance membership. Lessons 3, 6 and 9."},{"id":"b018","markdown":"### Step 8: Weeks 2–3. Build a 1-month buffer"},{"id":"b019","markdown":"Save one month of essential expenses in the savings account. Direct half of windfalls, bonuses or tax refunds there. Once complete, if debts above 30% exist, send all spare money to the highest rate while paying other minimums. Otherwise continue towards 3 months of essential spending. Lessons 5 and 6."},{"id":"b020","markdown":"### Step 9: Week 3. Check refinancing and card terms"},{"id":"b021","markdown":"For high-rate loans from 2024–2025, ask several banks about refinancing. Compare full costs and reject longer terms. Open card tariffs: balance interest, cashback and maintenance fees.\\nTo use a credit card without interest, take Guide 2. If unsure about always repaying fully and punctually, do not use it for everyday purchases. Lessons 5 and 9."},{"id":"b022","markdown":"### Step 10: Week 4. Claim tax deductions"},{"id":"b023","markdown":"Check the Federal Tax Service taxpayer account for prefilled deduction applications. Recall healthcare, education, sport and housing spending in 2023, 2024 and 2025. The 2023 deadline expires at the end of 2026. Create a folder for 2026 receipts, contracts and certificates. If you have children, check payroll’s standard deduction. Lesson 10."},{"id":"b024","markdown":"### Outcome"},{"id":"b025","markdown":"After 30 days you will have:"},{"id":"b026","markdown":"- Your hourly price and an understanding of where money goes."},{"id":"b027","markdown":"- Closed leaks."},{"id":"b028","markdown":"- Verified credit history and anti-fraud restrictions."},{"id":"b029","markdown":"- A debt repayment plan, if needed."},{"id":"b030","markdown":"- A savings account with automatic funding."},{"id":"b031","markdown":"- A month’s buffer or a clear path towards it."},{"id":"b032","markdown":"- Submitted or planned tax deductions."},{"id":"b033","markdown":"Repeat step 3 in a month and compare the figures. Afterwards, checking every 3–6 months is sufficient."}],"terms":[{"id":"kreditnaya-istoriya","term":"Credit history","definition":"A record of how you repaid loans. A poor or absent history means rejection or a rate above the market. An empty history is worse than a history of repaid loans."},{"id":"mfo","term":"Microfinance organisations (MFOs)","definition":"Companies lending to people who do not interest banks. After the banking-sector clean-up, their number in Russia exceeded 1000."},{"id":"nalogovyy-vychet","term":"Tax deduction","definition":"The state refunds part of the tax paid. Up to 260 000 RUB for buying an apartment, 13% for healthcare and education. Real money that people fail to claim because they do not know about it."},{"id":"psk","term":"Full cost of credit (PSK)","definition":"The equivalent of an effective interest rate: the real cost of a loan including every payment. Banks must disclose it, though in small print. The only honest comparison figure."},{"id":"refinansirovanie","term":"Refinancing","definition":"A new loan at a lower rate to repay an old one. It can help when the rate difference exceeds 1.5–2% and substantial time remains. It makes sense in the first half of the term."},{"id":"strakhovanie-vkladov","term":"Deposit insurance","definition":"A state guarantee to repay depositors up to a certain amount if a bank fails. In Russia, 1.4 million RUB per bank through the Deposit Insurance Agency."}],"quizzes":[],"officialSources":[]}')}}]);